<header class="page-header"><h1>Overset Fixer Pro</h1></header>

<p>Overset Fixer Pro is a script for Adobe InDesign that fixes overset text frames and overset table cells. It either reduces the text formatting within limits you set, or grows frames downward and makes table rows taller. One undo reverts the whole run.</p>

<p><a href="https://aescripts.com/overset-fixer-pro/">Free trial and full version on aescripts</a></p>

<p><iframe loading="lazy" allowfullscreen title="Overset Fixer Pro v2 for Adobe InDesign, overview video" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/k7VR0ixWUW4"></iframe></p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
<li>Text Adjustment Mode lowers tracking, font size and horizontal scale, one control at a time, until the text fits. Leading follows the font size at a ratio you set. Frames, rows and columns stay where they are.</li>
<li>Frame Expansion Mode grows text frames downward in steps. If you allow it, it also grows table rows that are set to Exactly. The text formatting is not changed.</li>
<li>It finds overset cells in tables, including nested tables.</li>
<li>One fix can push text into overset further down the same story, so the script scans the document again after each round, up to five rounds.</li>
<li>The summary at the end lists what was fixed, what was skipped and why, and what could not be resolved.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What to know before you run it</h2>
<ul>
<li>Text Adjustment Mode changes the whole story a frame belongs to. If a selected frame is threaded, text in the other frames of that story changes too. The script asks before it continues.</li>
<li>The changes are local formatting. Adjusted paragraphs show the override marker (+) beside their paragraph style name.</li>
<li>If the text still does not fit when every enabled control is at its limit, the original formatting is restored and the item is reported as unresolved.</li>
<li>Frame Expansion Mode only moves the bottom edge of a frame. Other page items do not move, so a grown frame can overlap something below it.</li>
<li>Review the layout after the run.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Trial</h2>
<p>The trial is the complete script with one limit: it applies up to 10 fixes per document. Detection and the summary are not limited, so you can see what it finds in your own files before buying.</p>

<h2>Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Adobe InDesign 2024 or later</li>
<li>macOS or Windows</li>
<li>A JSX script, run from the Scripts panel</li>
</ul>

